"mi-","H4310","HPi","who?"],["יִתֵּן","yiten","H5414","HVqi3ms","will he give"],["מוּתִי","muti","H4191","HVqcc/Sp1bs","died I"],["אֲנִי","'ani","H589","HPp1bs","I"],["תַחְתֶּיךָ","tachteikha","H8478","HNcmpc/Sp2ms","in place of you"],["אַבְשָׁלוֹם","'avshalom","H53","HNpm","O Absalom"],["בְּנִי","beni","H1121","HNcmsc/Sp1bs","son my"],["בְנִי","veni","H1121","HNcmsc/Sp1bs","son my"]],"x":[[10019004,10019004,8],[10012010,10012023,4],[19103013,19103013,4],[20010001,20010001,4],[20017025,20017025,4]],"xn":5}},"people":[{"id":"david_994","name":"David","also":"","summary":"Beloved, the eighth and youngest son of Jesse, a citizen of Bethlehem. His father seems to have been a man in humble life. His mother’s name is not recorded.","verses":896,"father":"Jesse","mother":"","v":[1,2,7,9,24]},{"id":"joab_1617","name":"Joab","also":"","summary":"One of the three sons of Zeruiah, David’s sister, and “captain of the host” during the whole of David’s reign (2 Sam. 2:13; 10:7; 11:1; 1 Kings 11:15).","verses":119,"father":"","mother":"Zeruiah","v":[2,5,10,11,12,14,15,16,20,21,22,29]},{"id":"zeruiah_3055","name":"Zeruiah","also":"","summary":"Stricken of the Lord, David’s sister, and the mother of Abishai, Joab, and Asahel (1 Chr. 2:16), who were the three leading heroes of David’s army, and being his nephews, they were admitted to the closest companionship with him.","verses":25,"father":"Nahash","mother":"","v":[2]},{"id":"abishai_50","name":"Abishai","also":"","summary":"Father of (i.e., “desirous of”) a gift, the eldest son of Zeruiah, David’s sister. He was the brother of Joab and Asahel (2 Sam. 2:18; 1 Chr. 2:16).","verses":24,"father":"","mother":"Zeruiah","v":[2,5,12]},{"id":"ittai_656","name":"Ittai","also":"","summary":"A native of Gath, a Philistine, who had apparently the command of the six hundred heroes who formed David’s band during his wanderings (2 Sam. 15:19-22; comp. 1 Sam. 23:13; 27:2; 30:9, 10).","verses":6,"father":"","mother":"","v":[2,5,12]},{"id":"absalom_59","name":"Absalom","also":"Abishalom","summary":"Father of peace; i.e., “peaceful” David’s son by Maacah (2 Sam. 3:3; comp. 1 Kings 1:6). He was noted for his personal beauty and for the extra-ordinary profusion of the hair of his head (2 Sam. 14:25,26).","verses":91,"father":"David","mother":"Maacah","v":[5,9,10,12,14,15,17,18,29,32,33]},{"id":"ephraim_1206","name":"Ephraim","also":"","summary":"Double fruitfulness (“for God had made him fruitful in the land of his affliction”). The second son of Joseph, born in Egypt (Gen. 41:52; 46:20).","verses":160,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Asenath","v":[6]},{"id":"zadok_2973","name":"Zadok","also":"","summary":"A son of Ahitub, of the line of Eleazer (2 Sam. 8:17; 1 Chr. 24:3), high priest in the time of David (2 Sam. 20:25) and Solomon (1 Kings 4:4).","verses":40,"father":"Ahitub","mother":"","v":[19,22,27]},{"id":"ahimaaz_144","name":"Ahimaaz","also":"","summary":"The son and successor of Zadok in the office of high priest (1 Chr. 6:8, 53). On the occasion of the revolt of Absalom he remained faithful to David, and was of service to him in conveying to him tidings of the proceedings of Absalom in Jerusalem (2 Sam. 15:24-37; 17:15-21).","verses":13,"father":"Zadok","mother":"","v":[19,22,23,27,28,29]},{"id":"cushi_964","name":"Cushi","also":"","summary":"Then Joab said to a Cushite.","verses":5,"father":"","mother":"","v":[21,22,23,31,32]}],"places":[{"id":"forest-of-ephraim_1294","name":"Forest of Ephraim","kind":"Region","lat":32.38111,"lon":35.76472,"summary":"Added from Digital Manna places-1273 (LPF sync 2026-10-13)","verses":2,"v":[6,8]},{"id":"valley_of_shaveh_692","name":"valley of Shaveh","kind":"Valley","lat":31.77744,"lon":35.23494,"summary":"Valley of the plain the ancient name of the “king’s dale”, or Kidron, on the north side of Jerusalem (Gen. 14:17).","verses":2,"v":[18]}],"events":[{"id":"reign_of_david_159","title":"Reign of David","year":-1055,"summary":"Passage: 2 Samuel 2:1–24:25. People: David. Place